WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.213
Are you wondering how to reduce your return rates?

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:06.072
Well, here's 7 best practices

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.835
to help reduce returns.

00:00:07.835 --> 00:00:09.343
Let's get started.

00:00:14.464 --> 00:00:18.966
Number 1: Adopting a liberal returns policy.

00:00:18.966 --> 00:00:22.185
A liberal ecommerce returns policy, 

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:25.960
also sometimes called a customer-centric returns policy

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.754
empowers the customer to purchase a product with confidence

00:00:29.754 --> 00:00:31.207
and peace of mind, 

00:00:31.207 --> 00:00:34.083
knowing they have the option to return it later.

00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:36.351
It may seem counterproductive

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:39.184
to incorporate a liberal returns policy

00:00:39.184 --> 00:00:41.921
when you’re trying to reduce your product returns, 

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:44.707
but a customer-focused returns policy 

00:00:44.707 --> 00:00:47.084
can actually help you prevent returns, 

00:00:47.084 --> 00:00:48.966
and boost sales.

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:53.603
Number 2: Segmenting your customer database.

00:00:53.603 --> 00:00:58.688
Personas or traits developed by looking at careful considerations 

00:00:58.688 --> 00:01:01.357
and analysis of your customer database

00:01:01.357 --> 00:01:04.317
are much more accurate than general depictions

00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:06.198
of high-risk customers.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.659
Segmenting to prevent returns 

00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:12.409
is not much different from segmenting for marketing purposes. 

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:14.516
At the rudimentary level,

00:01:14.516 --> 00:01:18.868
you’re just trying to identify trends, behaviors, traits,

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.747
and other useful metrics 

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.546
to make smarter decisions moving forward. 

00:01:23.546 --> 00:01:26.007
The effectiveness of this strategy

00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:29.214
is dependent on the depth of metrics you’ve gathered 

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:32.779
and your overall returns and handling process.

00:01:32.779 --> 00:01:37.342
Number 3: Incorporating high-quality visuals.

00:01:37.342 --> 00:01:41.259
Considering that 23% of product returns

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:44.506
are because of inaccurate depictions of the product,

00:01:44.506 --> 00:01:46.436
high-quality visuals

00:01:46.436 --> 00:01:48.946
that provide detailed views of items

00:01:48.946 --> 00:01:51.464
become crucial to bridge the gap

00:01:51.464 --> 00:01:56.637
between the consumer’s expectations and the reality of the product.

00:01:56.637 --> 00:02:01.811
Number 4: Customer feedback and hassle-free returns.

00:02:01.811 --> 00:02:05.189
Gathering feedback for a product return 

00:02:05.189 --> 00:02:07.442
can be a tedious process, 

00:02:07.442 --> 00:02:10.402
both for the retailer and customer, 

00:02:10.402 --> 00:02:11.964
but nevertheless, 

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.945
relevant customer feedback

00:02:13.945 --> 00:02:17.589
allows retailers to improve the overall brand experience

00:02:17.589 --> 00:02:19.787
and understand various defects 

00:02:19.787 --> 00:02:22.254
in their returns management process.

00:02:22.254 --> 00:02:25.672
By collecting customer feedback from product returns, 

00:02:25.672 --> 00:02:28.916
retailers are unlocking valuable insight

00:02:28.916 --> 00:02:30.245
into their products.

00:02:30.245 --> 00:02:34.349
Insights, which otherwise would not have been discovered.

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:39.260
Number 5: Data driven emails to prevent returns.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.636
Your marketing team and operations team 

00:02:42.636 --> 00:02:46.181
are fighting the same war and should complement each other.

00:02:46.181 --> 00:02:49.116
Having your marketing and sales team

00:02:49.116 --> 00:02:52.816
provide air support for your operations and logistics team

00:02:52.816 --> 00:02:56.225
is a good formula for increased productivity, 

00:02:56.225 --> 00:02:59.596
profit, and reduced churn and hassle.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.486
Using customer feedback

00:03:01.486 --> 00:03:03.083
and segmenting data,

00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:06.414
you can better identify which products are problematic 

00:03:06.414 --> 00:03:10.513
and which customers are likely to return certain items.

00:03:10.513 --> 00:03:14.861
Number 6: Incorporating customer reviews.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:18.779
Product reviews provide both considerable SEO 

00:03:18.779 --> 00:03:22.231
and sales benefits for ecommerce retailers,

00:03:22.231 --> 00:03:26.632
but let’s not forget that they also help reduce product returns.

00:03:26.632 --> 00:03:30.375
Product reviews empower customers to make better, 

00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:32.687
more well-informed decisions, 

00:03:32.687 --> 00:03:35.480
which ultimately lead to fewer regrets.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.576
Incorporating product reviews

00:03:37.576 --> 00:03:40.735
is such an effective returns prevention strategy

00:03:40.735 --> 00:03:44.439
that PetCo reported that products with customer reviews 

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:47.715
had a 20.3% lower return rate

00:03:47.715 --> 00:03:49.324
than those that didn’t.

00:03:49.324 --> 00:03:51.841
And lastly, Number 7:

00:03:51.841 --> 00:03:55.413
Constant analysis and team incorporation.

00:03:55.413 --> 00:03:58.584
Although returns are a bitter pill to swallow, 

00:03:58.584 --> 00:04:02.408
ultimately— they provide retailers a complete view

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:06.062
of their customers, processes, and products. 

00:04:06.062 --> 00:04:08.399
One of the primary realizations

00:04:08.399 --> 00:04:09.787
retailers have 

00:04:09.787 --> 00:04:13.813
when they start to think of ways to reduce the volume of their product returns,

00:04:13.813 --> 00:04:18.037
is how important customer metrics and data can be.

00:04:18.037 --> 00:04:20.587
Learning as much as you possibly can 

00:04:20.587 --> 00:04:23.961
about your returns and exchanges process,

00:04:23.961 --> 00:04:26.074
in the top to bottom manner

00:04:26.074 --> 00:04:30.179
will arm you with the knowledge to make better business decisions.

